      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Loanhead grew from coal and oil shale mining, the Springfield paper mill began in 1742, and the town linked to the railway by 1874.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        24,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loanhead",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The former Bilston Glen Colliery, once employing 795 miners, was redeveloped into an industrial estate that now houses MacSween’s haggis factory and Police Scotland’s Communications Centre.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.scottish-places.info/towns/townfirst254.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Mavisbank House, a derelict Palladian mansion built in 1723, was featured on the BBC series Restoration in 2004.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loanhead",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
